#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1130 expect=noViolation domain=SUPPMH
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner 2026-10-12, verify on data first; PLAN-engine-gap-value-addressed Q7): SDTMIG 3.3 section 4.5.3.2 Example 1 (p. 56) as published - MHTERM with 500 characters, its continuation in SUPPMH as QNAM MHTERM1 and MHTERM2, both with the QLABEL of the original variable ('Reported Term for the Medical History'), which the IG prescribes: the long text is one value, so the label carries no suffix. Plus one unrelated qualifier. A conforming SUPPMH; the rule must not fire. Shape fixed in PLAN-stopped-rule-engine-fixes item 3 (SR4 / SR5): fires twice under the rule before its family-stem conjunct."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
dataset SUPPMH label="Supplemental Qualifiers for MH"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
12345 | MH | 99-123 | MHSEQ | 6 | MHTERM1 | Reported Term for the Medical History | 2nd ~200 chars of text, split between words | CRF |
12345 | MH | 99-123 | MHSEQ | 6 | MHTERM2 | Reported Term for the Medical History | last 100 or more chars of text | CRF |
12345 | MH | 99-124 | MHSEQ | 2 | MHOTHER | Other Medical History Detail | DETAIL | CRF |
